        "date": "2026-11-08T01:28:31Z"
      },
      "message": "fix(motion): a D-flat that faces the axis vouches for its roundness\n\nSince #223 the axis fit's roundness readings use only facets whose\nnormal lines meet the axis within the concurrency tolerance, which\nkeeps an off-axis boss from lending its bearings - but a D-flat's facets\nmiss that line by part of the flat's width, so a single-band D-flat bar\nread \"share no rotation axis\" and rotary_dflat went red on main. A facet\nsquare to the axis whose line misses by less than half its own size\nfaces the axis (the foot of the axis is on the face): its normal now\ncounts in the coarseness gate and the point-share pencil check.\n\nFixes #246\n\nCo-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>",
